---
source: https://www.statesman.com/story/lifestyle/food/2020/12/18/all-your-christmas-ham-needs-cherry-bourbon-barbecue-sauce/3888883001/
author: Ray Sheehan
total time: 30 minutes
tags:
  - sauce
---

In a #medium saucepan{}, combine @unsweetened cherry juice{1%cup}, @honey{1/3%cup}, @ketchup{1%cup}, @light brown sugar{1/3%cup}, @tomato paste{1/4%cup}, @cider vinegar{1/4%cup}, @bourbon{3%Tbsp}, @hot sauce{2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1.5%tsp}, @freshly ground black pepper{1%tsp}, @granulated garlic{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, @dry mustard{1/2%tsp}, and @celery salt{1/2%tsp}. Bring to a gentle boil over medium heat, stirring to dissolve the sugar.

Lower heat to low and simmer until slightly thickened, 20 to ~{25%minutes}, stirring frequently.

Let cool, transfer to a #jar{} and store in the refrigerator for up to a month.
